---
/** The privacy page, in English. The frame is PrivacyPage. */
import PrivacyPage from '../../components/pages/PrivacyPage.astro';
---

<PrivacyPage>
	<p>
		This is a personal site. It has no accounts, no forms, no comments and no
		analytics. I don’t collect your name, your email address or anything you do
		here, and there’s no database behind this page for any of it to go into.
	</p>

	<h2>What reaches other people</h2>
	<p>
		Everything on these pages, fonts included, comes from this site, so your
		browser doesn’t contact anyone else to show them.
	</p>
	<p>
		<strong>Hosting.</strong> The site runs on Vercel, whose servers keep ordinary
		request logs, which include IP addresses. I don’t read them and I don’t build
		anything from them.
	</p>

	<h2>Links away from here</h2>
	<p>
		Links to the App Store, Google Play, GitHub and the projects themselves go to
		services with their own privacy policies, and this one stops at the edge of
		this site.
	</p>

	<h2>Storage on your device</h2>
	<p>
		If you use the light and dark toggle, your choice is saved in
		<code>localStorage</code> under the key <code>theme</code>. It never leaves your
		browser and I can’t read it. Clearing site data removes it.
	</p>
	<p>
		The site also hides seven Moons. To keep track of them, it saves which ones
		you’ve found and how far you’ve got with the rest: the project pages you’ve
		visited, the school and game cards you’ve opened, and the headline endings
		you’ve seen. It also saves whether the chime that plays when you find one is
		on or off. All of that starts on your first visit, stays in your browser
		under the key <code>moons</code>, and never reaches me. Clearing site data
		removes it, and so does this button:
		<button type="button" class="forget-moons" data-forget>Forget my Moons</button>
	</p>
	<p>
		The chime is made in your browser, so no sound file is loaded for it.
	</p>
	<p>
		Your language isn’t saved anywhere. The site is in English at its usual
		addresses and in Portuguese under <code>/pt-BR/</code>, and the switch in the
		header is a plain link between the two.
	</p>

	<h2>Asking</h2>
	<p>
		If something here is unclear, write to
		<a href="mailto:me@enriccogemha.dev">me@enriccogemha.dev</a>.
	</p>
</PrivacyPage>
